From: Pharma360 QA Team
Subject: [PATCH 008/07] Fix frontend port mapping to match nginx config
Date: 2026-11-01

This patch fixes the frontend container port mapping. The frontend.conf
listens on port 8080, but the docker-compose.yml was mapping 3000:80.

The frontend.Dockerfile uses nginxinc/nginx-unprivileged:alpine which serves
on port 8080 (as configured in frontend.conf), so we need to map 8080:8080.

---
 docker/docker-compose.yml | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/docker/docker-compose.yml b/docker/docker-compose.yml
index abc1234..def5678 100644
--- a/docker/docker-compose.yml
+++ b/docker/docker-compose.yml
@@ -93,7 +93,7 @@ services:
     depends_on:
       pharma360-backend:
         condition: service_healthy
     ports:
-      - "${FRONTEND_PORT:-3000}:80"
+      - "${FRONTEND_PORT:-8080}:8080"
     networks:
       - pharma360-network
     healthcheck:
---
To apply this patch:
  cd /workspace/github__DuDuEZN__Pharma-360
  patch -p1 < patches/008-fix-frontend-port-mapping.patch

OR manually apply:
  1. Edit docker/docker-compose.yml
  2. Change line 96 from:
     - "${FRONTEND_PORT:-3000}:80"
     to:
     - "${FRONTEND_PORT:-8080}:8080"

Note: This change is necessary because:
- frontend.conf has: listen 8080
- The nginx container serves on port 8080
- The reverse proxy (pharma360-nginx) proxies to http://pharma360-frontend:8080
- So the frontend container must expose port 8080
